WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.260
Between 2000 and 2023, measles
vaccination averted an estimated

2
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.340
60 million deaths worldwide.

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.850
Health agencies aim for 95 per
cent coverage with 2 doses.

4
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:18.200
In 2023, global coverage of the
second dose was 74 per cent.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.240
And each vaccinated person also lowers
the chance that others catch the disease.

6
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.800
So if a vaccine also protects
the people around you,

7
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.240
why might too few people get one?

8
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.070
In this mission, you'll
draw the benefit to society

9
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.280
as its own curve, and
find the best quantity.

10
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.550
Then you'll turn up the
spillover in a graph

11
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.150
lab and see which curves move.

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.660
Your mission: explain why
too few people get one,

13
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.640
and how society loses out.
